# Saffron Gym is the teleporter-pad maze: 32 warps, all self-referential
# SAFFRON_GYM -> SAFFRON_GYM, dividing the floor into nine sealed 6x5 cells
# joined only by pads. Sabrina sits in cell (y=7..11, x=7..12) whose ONLY pad
# is (11,11), so no pad chain is needed once a worker is inside -- but nothing
# on map 178 was guided at all, so workers reached her room by luck and then
# wandered it (reported live on env 88 at (7,7)).
#
# Generated offline by BFS over the ROM's own warp table plus the FACILITY
# collision data: cell-level BFS picks each cell's outbound pad, then a
# within-cell BFS gives every tile the first action toward it. Entrance
# (17,8) is four hops out -- (15,11) -> (15,15) -> (5,15) -> (5,1) -> lands
# on (11,11) in Sabrina's cell. Every cell is covered, so a worker dropped
# anywhere by a pad is immediately back on route. Each tuple is
# (map, y, x, action); pad warps keep map_id 178 so they carry no
# destination_map. Sabrina's own tile (8,9) is deliberately unruled, and the
# talk tile (9,9) is owned by the interaction rule below.
#
# Pads are LAUNCH tiles, never through-tiles. The first version of
# this table routed cell 8 straight across the pad at (17,15) on its
# way to (15,15), which teleported the entire 96-worker swarm into
# cell 6 and pinned it there. Each cell's search therefore cuts every
# pad but its own target, and each non-target pad gets a single
# step-off rule so a worker that LANDS on one rejoins the route.
